{"results":[{"url":"https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/telangana/hmwssb-warns-residents-against-water-wastage-threatens-to-disconnect-services/article71491795.ece","final_url":"https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/telangana/hmwssb-warns-residents-against-water-wastage-threatens-to-disconnect-services/article71491795.ece","title":"HMWSSB warns residents against water wastage, threatens to disconnect services","description":"HMWS&SB warns residents against water wastage, threatening disconnection of services for repeat offenders amid rising penalties.","language":"en","text":"You are logged in\n\nLoading...\n\nYou don’t have any Active Subscription.\n\nSubscribe now\n\nSubscribed with another email? Logout and Login with that one.\n\nYour active subscription(s)\n\nAccount subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials,\nOpinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription\n\nProducts you've access to\n\nAdditional Subscription Benefits\n\n* eBooks\n* Webinars\n* Newsletters\n* Games\n* Monthly Digest\n\nAccount Settings\n\n* Go to My Account\n* Bookmarks\n* Manage Subscriptions\n\nNeed help with your subscription?\n\n* customersupport@thehindu.co.in\n* 1800 102 1878\n\n# HMWSSB warns residents against water wastage, threatens to disconnect services\n\nPublished - September 21, 2026 07:45 pm IST - HYDERABAD\n\nThe Hindu Bureau\n\nSEE ALL\nRemove\n\nThe Hyderabad Metropolitan Water Supply & Sewerage Board (HMWS&SB) has issued serious warning against water wastage, after imposing penalties in five such instances on Monday. Second time offenders will attract disconnection of water supply, it warned.\n\nAll the five penalised were residents of Jubilee Hills, and found to have been wasting water, during inspections conducted by the Board officials.\n\nThe inspections will be intensified in the coming days, and second time offenders will be penalised through disconnection of water supply, the note warned.\n\nUsing drinking water to wash floor and vehicles, leaving the tap open, and not shutting down the pump set even after overhead tank overflows are some of the instances of water wastage, as shared by the Board.\n\nDespite awareness campaigns and warnings, the users are still found resorting to the same practices, calling for penalties. The penalties which had started with just ₹1000 per instance, have over the time risen to ₹5,000, then ₹10,000 and now ₹20,000. Still the violations continue to persist. the note said.\n\nLeakages in the water supply network too will be plugged by officials within 24 hours of identification, and in case of dereliction of duties, action will be taken against officials and staff too. The water board’s drinking water pipeline extends to 15,000 kilometres in the city, to plug leakages in which, a special action plan is being be taken up. The officials have been directed to identify locations with frequent leakages and provide permanent solutions.\n\nPublished - September 21, 2026 07:45 pm IST\n\n* Copy link\n* Facebook\n* Twitter\n* Telegram\n* LinkedIn\n* WhatsApp\n* Reddit\n\nSEE ALL\nRemove\n\n0 / 0\n\nSign in to unlock member-only benefits!\n\n* Access 10 free stories every month\n* Save stories to read later\n* Access to comment on every story\n* Sign-up/manage your newsletter subscriptions with a single click\n* Get notified by email for early access to discounts & offers on our products\n\nLooks like you are already logged in from more than 5 devices!\n\nTo continue logging in, remove at least one device from the below list\n\n\n\nTerms & conditions  |  Institutional Subscriber\n\n${ ind + 1 }\n${ device }Last active - ${ la }\n\n### Comments\n\nComments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines  for posting your comments.\n\nWe have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle.","author":"The Hindu Bureau","published_date":"2026-09-21T19:45:00+05:30","latency_ms":528.2859459985048,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}